    "problem_statement": "Query.remove() method returns None instead of self\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `Query.remove()` method is returning `None` instead of returning `self`, breaking method chaining functionality.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport furl\n\n# This should work but raises AttributeError\nf = furl.furl('http://example.com?a=1&b=2')\nresult = f.query.remove('a').remove('b')  # AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'remove'\n\n# This also fails\nq = furl.Query('a=1&b=2')\nchained = q.remove('a').remove('b')  # AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'remove'\n```\n\nThe expected behavior is that `remove()` should return the Query instance to allow method chaining, similar to other methods in the API."
  }
